npm init -y creates a package.json file. This file records your project’s name, scripts, and dependencies (the libraries it needs). Anyone who gets your project can run npm install and get everything.

What each part does:

require('express') imports the library.
express() creates your app (the server).
app.get('/', ...) defines a route: when someone sends a GET request to /, run this function.
req is the incoming request (data from the client). res is the response you send back.
app.listen starts the server on port 3000.

Run it with npm run dev, then visit http://localhost:3000 in your browser. You should see your message.